WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.488
Sixth, automation.

2
00:00:01.488 --> 00:00:06.876
No rule requires an API, but Book
08's operating model depends on one.

3
00:00:06.876 --> 00:00:11.167
Every object, addresses, DHCP,
DNS configuration and DNS data,

4
00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:16.318
should be reachable through a documented
API, so infrastructure as code,

5
00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:20.524
ITSM workflows, certificate
automation and pipelines all

6
00:00:20.524 --> 00:00:24.387
go through the same authority
and the same audit trail.

7
00:00:24.387 --> 00:00:27.918
Automation runs as
non-interactive service accounts,

8
00:00:27.918 --> 00:00:32.862
held to the same roles and scopes as people
and unable to log in to the console.

9
00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:37.497
Expect supported Terraform and
Ansible, ITSM actions that reserve

10
00:00:37.497 --> 00:00:41.800
an address or register a record,
and a path for existing scripts.

11
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.470
Check how the API authenticates;
NIOS, for example,

12
00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:51.937
added OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect
for its API in release 9.1.

13
00:00:51.937 --> 00:00:55.250
Seventh, logging to the
SIEM, sized for the load.

14
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.315
The requirement here is
M-26-14's retention:

15
00:00:58.315 --> 00:01:02.520
logs searchable for six months
and retrievable for a year,

16
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:08.738
with synchronized timestamps, available to
the agency's security operations center.

17
00:01:08.738 --> 00:01:11.269
The name layer contributes query logs,

18
00:01:11.269 --> 00:01:14.750
lease history, policy hits
and the change audit trail.

19
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.163
Capacity is where designs fail.

20
00:01:17.163 --> 00:01:21.181
Microsoft measured about five
percent degradation from

21
00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:25.199
full Windows DNS query logging
at 100,000 queries a second.

22
00:01:25.199 --> 00:01:30.085
NIOS reporting appliances have daily
ingest limits, and after five overruns

23
00:01:30.085 --> 00:01:35.200
in a rolling thirty days the reporting
functions lock until support intervenes.

24
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.027
And dnstap on NIOS drops
records rather than

25
00:01:38.027 --> 00:01:40.625
buffering them when the receiver is down.

26
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:43.990
Size for peak, and test
with the SIEM unreachable.
